From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:36:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] hunt stress0: any cut that is not the partition's is
 flagged, and the loop counts the ones met without a failure

The provenance check flagged only a cut behind the walk; a cut ahead of it
asserts nothing and answers wrong, so it now flags any cut that differs from
the partition's own for the key. The forced cut schedule takes the seal
thread's snapshot and the handles' sharing off so the stale cut is reached
every run, and the loop has an ok-stale-cut class and an alternating
two-binary script for pairing a scratch fix against the head.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011ZkLidS5BYuaBXVcvPAkdd
